{
  "title": "Family",
  "note": "Japanese has two sets of family words: plain humble ones for your own family when talking to others (父, 母, 兄) and polite ones for someone else's family (お父さん, お母さん, お兄さん). For people and animals, \"there is\" or \"have\" is います, and the person counted takes が: 兄が二人います \"I have two older brothers.\"",
